course: dictionary
lesson: 9312
title: Speed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Speed tells you how fast something moves: how far it goes in a certain time. A car that travels 60 kilometres in one hour has a speed of 60 kilometres per hour. Speed can also mean quickness, as in «with great speed».
explain: Speed is also a doing word. To speed is to move fast, and to speed up is to go faster. «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, which speeds up the heart» means the heart beats faster. To slow down is the opposite.
explain: Context helps you see which meaning fits. «A swing is fastest at the bottom and slowest at the top» is about how fast the swing moves, so speed is a noun there. Check by swapping in your meaning: fastest and slowest show that speed means how fast something goes.
fact: Speed is how fast something moves: the distance it covers in a certain time.
fact: Speed is measured in miles per hour, kilometres per hour, or metres per second.
fact: Distance = speed × time, so a higher speed covers more distance in the same time.
fact: «Speeding» means driving faster than the law allows.
fact: «Speed bump» and «high-speed train» use speed as a noun, and «at full speed» means as fast as possible.
exercise: «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed.» In this sentence, what is speed? | *How fast something moves | A kind of machine | A type of rope | A sort of heat
exercise: «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, which speeds up the heart.» What does speeds up mean? | *Goes faster | Stops beating | Turns cold | Goes slower
exercise: A driver who goes faster than the law allows is doing what? | Parking | Waving | Stopping | *Speeding
test: «The bike rode down the hill at full speed.» What does at full speed mean? | Backwards | *As fast as it can go | Without a rider | Very slowly
test: A train travels 100 miles in 2 hours. What is its speed? | 2 miles per hour | 200 miles per hour | *50 miles per hour | 102 miles per hour
exam: Which pair of words means the same as to go faster? | slow down | stop | sit still | *speed up
